Hmm, but note: the final `msg(LOG_INFO, "Size of exported file/device is %llu"...)` at the end of setupexport — my early return would skip that. For consistency, log the size inside the branch and then return true.

Also, the readonly fallback logic: for plain files, if opening O_RDWR fails, retry O_RDONLY and set F_AUTOREADONLY. In treefiles, there's no per-export open at setup time. If the underlying medium is actually read-only, writes will fail at runtime with EROFS. That's acceptable — but should we set F_AUTOREADONLY for treefiles when F_READONLY? No, let's keep it simple.

