steps.message:
Found a real bug! When multiple clients connect simultaneously (nbd-server forks per connection), each child process runs setupexport. The `stat` and `mkdir` in my code race against each other:

1. Child A: stat() fails (directory doesn't exist yet)
2. Child B: stat() fails
3. Child A: mkdir succeeds
4. Child B: mkdir fails with EEXIST → treats this as a fatal error!

Because of `if (mkdir(...) < 0)` — it needs to tolerate EEXIST. This is the same classic race that this feature (the reason the mutex exists in the API) should handle. Each connection is a separate process (nbd-server forks per client), so an in-process mutex can't help here — we have to tolerate EEXIST.

Fix in setupexport:

```c
if (mkdir(client->exportname, 0700) < 0 && errno != EEXIST) {
```

But in that case, EEXIST might mean "an existing file that isn't a directory." So after EEXIST, check that it's a directory:

```c
if (stat(client->exportname, &st) < 0) {
	if (mkdir(client->exportname, 0700) < 0 && errno != EEXIST) {
		error...
		return false;
	}
	if (stat(client->exportname, &st) < 0 || !S_ISDIR(st.st_mode)) {
		error "not a directory"...
		return false;
	}
} else if (!S_ISDIR(st.st_mode)) {
	...
}
```

Cleaner structure:

```c
/* The block files of a treefiles export live in a tree of
 * directories below the export name, so the export name itself
 * must be a directory */
if (mkdir(client->exportname, 0700) < 0 && errno != EEXIST) {
	error "Could not create treefiles directory %s: %m"
	return false;
}
if (stat(client->exportname, &st) < 0 || !S_ISDIR(st.st_mode)) {
	error "%s is not a directory"
	return false;
}
```

mkdir first (EEXIST tolerated, to avoid TOCTOU), then stat+S_ISDIR check. Note: mkdir_path in treefiles.c already tolerates EEXIST — good (concurrent child processes creating TREE directories at the same time). open with O_CREAT tolerates EEXIST. unlink tolerates ENOENT. So the entire tree machinery is multi-process-safe except for this one spot.

Let's apply the fix.
Found a real bug: nbd-server forks per connection, so when multiple clients connect simultaneously each child runs setupexport, and the `stat`→`mkdir` sequence races — the losing child fails with EEXIST. Fix: mkdir first tolerating EEXIST, then validate it's a directory.

